## The gate's own mechanism

| Probe | `content` returned |
|---|---|
| Issued exactly as `puc2_preflight` issues it (no `return_content`) | {{ puc2_diag_findings.gate_blind_spot.gate_style_has_content }} (HTTP {{ puc2_diag_findings.gate_blind_spot.gate_style_http }}) |
| Same request with `return_content: true` | {{ puc2_diag_findings.gate_blind_spot.diag_has_content }} |

**{{ puc2_diag_verdict.gate_mechanism }}**

`ansible.builtin.uri` only puts the response body in `content` when
`return_content: true` is set — otherwise the key is absent and
`registered.content | default('')` yields the empty string. `X in ''` is False
for every X, which is what the gate reported, whatever MISP and IRIS actually
contain.

